    flip_trigger: "a guard -- an else-less `if` heading a tail spine with a following statement, whose arm ends in a return -- lowers to Branch(c, arm, rest of the spine) (v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_guard_branch). What still refuses here is an else-less `if` whose arm falls through with no return: it is a statement run for effect with no value, which v2 core does not model as a statement; flips if that is modeled (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode else_less_if_statement_has_no_lowered_form)"
  },
  CauseOwnership {
    cause: ^body_lowering_reason_return_not_in_tail_position,
    grain: FatalGrain,
    lane: SharedSelfHostCriticalPath,
    flip_trigger: "a return lowers only in tail position -- a function body's tail, an arm of a tail if or match, an admitted guard's arm -- read top-down from the raw parse; every other return refuses here, located at it, rather than lowering to its operand as the value of whatever block held it (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode return_lowered_as_its_operand_outside_the_function_tail). A let whose value is a match with returning arms, heading a tail spine with exactly ONE binding arm, lowers to that match with the rest of the spine under the binding arm (v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_let_match_exit_join). A return out of any other non-tail position (a let value otherwise, an operand, a loop body) is early exit through a continuation, which v2 core does not model; flips only if that is modeled. Count on the PR"
  },
